// error: what is passed for `body` of `isolate` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches `cache`, a module-level value holding a `Buffer[int]`, which is mutable; an immutable copy (`toVector`) is sendable
// error: what is passed for `body` of `isolate` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches the object `Tally`, whose field `count` is a `var`; make it a `val`
// error: what is passed for `body` of `isolate` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but through `Loud.next` it reaches `hits`, a module-level `var`, which every thread would share; share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex` held in a `val`
// error: what is passed for `f` of `Isolated.with` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches `hits`, a module-level `var`, which every thread would share; share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex` held in a `val`
// error: what is passed for `make` of `wrapped` is isolated, so nothing it runs may reach module-level mutable state, but it reaches `hits`, a module-level `var`, which every thread would share; share it through an `Atomic` or a `Mutex` held in a `val`
// More of what an `isolate` body or a `with` function may not reach: a `lazy val` holding a buffer,
// an object with a `var`, a module-level `var` behind a call through a trait (every implementation the
// call may reach counts), a `with` function writing a module-level `var`, and what is passed for a
// user's own `@isolating` parameter. Module-level values that are immutable and sendable are read
// freely: an integer, a vector, an object of `val`s, an atomic; and so is a local `var` of the
// calling code.
import avin.actors.{Isolated, isolate}
import avin.threads.Atomic

var hits = 0
lazy val cache = Buffer[int]()
val sizes = Vector(1, 2, 3)
val seen = Atomic[int](0)

object Tally
    var count = 0

object Fixed
    val most = 3

trait Source
    next() -> int

class Quiet(): Source
    override next() -> int = 1

class Loud(): Source
    override next() -> int
        hits += 1
        hits

wrapped[T](@isolating make: -> T) -> Isolated[T] = isolate(make)

main()
    var local = 0
    val ok = isolate
        local += sizes(0) + Fixed.most + seen.add(1)
        Buffer[int]()
    val a = isolate(cache.size)
    val b = isolate(Tally.count)
    val c = isolate
        val s: Source = Quiet()
        s.next()
    ok.with(buf -> hits += buf.size)
    val d = wrapped(hits)
